      Enters a comment to the SysOp.  The message is addressed to SysOp and
      is always a private message.
@X0F
   Description
@X03
      When you have a question about the system you will usually want to
      leave a message to the SysOp.  PCBoard provides a method by which you
      can easily enter a message to the SysOp without worrying who the
      message should be addressed to.  Before the actually leaving the
      message, you will be asked to confirm that you wish to leave a comment
      to the SysOp.  If you answer with a "Y" then you will be taken directly
      into the message editor.

      When the message is saved it will be placed into the current conference
      unless this system is configured to Force COMMENTS-to-the-Sysop into
      Main (Conference #0).

      See the help for (E)nter a Message for further information.
@XFF
